lychee (0.24.2-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pin the Rust toolchain to 1.98.0. Upstream's rust-toolchain.toml says
    channel = "stable", which records whichever compiler happened to be current on
    the build date rather than pinning one, so the published source would stop
    rebuilding to these bytes at the next Rust release. The binary is unchanged,
    verified byte-identical to the previous revision.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 13:54:07 +0200

lychee (0.24.2-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Declare the git build dependency. The build has always shelled out to git
    and only worked because the builder image ships it for cloning.
  * Build reproducibly: identical bytes across build path, hostname, locale,
    timezone, umask, CPU count and file ordering.
  * Record the Rust toolchain among the build dependencies, so the build
    can be reproduced from its .buildinfo.
  * Publish this version's source package and build record at
    buildinfos.pkg.haus, so anyone can reproduce the build and check it.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:38:12 +0200

lychee (0.24.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release, from 0.15.1: upstream moved to workspace-prefixed
    release tags (lychee-v*), so package.conf now tracks that scheme
  * Build-Depends: cmake for aws-lc-sys; drop libssl-dev, upstream moved
    from OpenSSL to rustls and openssl-sys is no longer in the lock file
  * Depends: ca-certificates. rustls loads the trust store at client
    construction and aborts when it is empty, so on a system without it
    lychee fails before doing any work, --offline included

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:14:59 +0200
